Ryujinx SPIR-V back end: emit "else if" chains (AstBlockType.ElseIf) as nested selections.
Without this, the false edge of the If before an ElseIf goes straight to the merge block and every
ElseIf/Else after it becomes unreachable code. See docs/nvn/TRANSLATOR.md, "else if chains".
Also a loop cap: every loop of a function leaves once its back edges, counted in one per-invocation
variable, reach N. Default 4096 for graphics stages (a runaway per-pixel loop in OoT's material shaders
took the GPU to TDR / device lost minutes into the first scene) and for task/mesh programs (translated as compute; OoT task fd8debac
runs 2^27 rounds while the data it counts is not built yet), off for compute; NXRT_HARNESS_LOOP_CAP=N overrides (0 = off).
Applied at build time by translator/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader.csproj to a copy in private/build; the
checkout in private/third_party stays untouched. The Ryujinx code in the context lines is MIT.
Also the task/mesh hooks of tools/shaders/ampere/frontend/AmpereMesh.cs (declarations after DeclareAll, execution model and modes,
the epilogue at the end of main, every global in the entry point).
